threads.body:
Suggestion (not blocking): `readAllBytes()` on a named pipe (FIFO) throws `IOException: Illegal seek` on JDK 21. It calls `position()`, which does an `lseek` that returns `ESPIPE` on a FIFO. I reproduced it with both `Files.newInputStream(fifo)` and `new FileInputStream(fifo)` on 21.0.7. Both work on 17 and 25.

The HTTP scenarios all run on 25/27, so nothing hits this today. But `scenarios/database/java` compiles `scenario-support` with a Java 21 toolchain for HBase, so a future Java 21 OBI scenario would fail with `waiting at the gate: Illegal seek`. A plain read loop works on every JDK we build with:

```java
var received = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
byte[] buffer = new byte[8];
for (int n; (n = pipe.read(buffer)) != -1; ) {
  received.write(buffer, 0, n);
}
```

